CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
duplicate label
CONVERSION ERROR
--
The disallowed patterns are the point of this test. Repeating
__CPROVER_ASYNC_1 within a function is well defined -- convert_label matches
the prefix and turns the labelled statement into a thread block, never a goto
target -- but typecheck_label rejected it as a duplicate label, so the program
failed with CONVERSION ERROR before any verification happened. Seven tests in
this directory are written this way.
